    "kind": "switching fabric",
    "note": "Vendor 132 Gbps non-blocking fabric across 30 ports (26 x 1G + 4 x 10G = 66 Gbit/s each way); forwarding rate 98.21 Mpps, line rate."
  },
  "poe": {
    "budgetW": 480,
    "sourceUrl": "https://www.downloads.netgear.com/files/GDC/M4250/M4250_Datasheet.pdf",
    "note": "480 W across 24 PoE+ ports (20 W per port on average), 180 W more than the SFP-only-uplink M4250-26G4F-PoE+ with the same 24-copper-port block - the 10G uplinks and the larger supply come together."
  },
  "notes": "M4250 series common platform: 16K MAC addresses, 4K ARP/NDP entries, 4K VLANs, static routes (894 IPv4 / 126 IPv6) plus RIP (32 IPv4), DHCP server (2K leases), sFlow, SNMP, console/telnet/SSH CLI and the AV web GUI. The 10G-uplink member of the 26-port family: same 24 PoE+ copper ports and 2 non-PoE copper ports as the M4250-26G4F-PoE+, but the four cages are 1G/10G SFP+ rather than 1G SFP and the fabric is 132 Gbps rather than 60. Sources: datasheet https://www.downloads.netgear.com/files/GDC/M4250/M4250_Datasheet.pdf and https://kb.netgear.com/000064904/NETGEAR-AV-Line-of-Fully-Managed-Switches-M4250-Series."
